---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";
import StylingHooks from "../../../components/StylingHooks.astro";
import { selectNativeTree, selectTree } from "../../../demos/select";
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from "../../../i18n";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/vanilla`;

const t = useTranslations(getLocale(Astro.url));

const styles = `@import "@skryensya/core/patterns/anchored.css";
@import "@skryensya/core/components/select.css";`;

const nativeInstall = `pnpm add @skryensya/core`;

const js = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";
import { mountIcons } from "@skryensya/vanilla/icon";
import { lucideIcons } from "@skryensya/icons-lucide";

// Icons are authored as <span data-sk-icon> placeholders;
// mountIcons replaces them with the <svg> of the linked set.
mountIcons(document, lucideIcons);

await initComponents();`;

const listen = `document
  .getElementById("plan")
  .addEventListener("sk-value-change", (event) => {
    console.log(event.detail.value); // ["pro"]
  });`;

const forms = `<div
  class="sk-select"
  data-sk-select
  id="plan"
>
  <!-- Optional: causes the Select to be sent in a form, and is what
       which is left without JS. Your <option> have to match
       the items, or the enhancer strips. -->
  <select data-sk-select-hidden name="plan">
    <option value="starter">Starter</option>
    <option value="pro">Pro</option>
  </select>
  …
</div>`;

---

<Base
  title="Select"
  description="Select: A machine-enhanced listbox, for Vanilla and React."
>
  <h1>Select</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The main selector when the interaction needs typeahead, highlight, controlled popup and positioning. <code>Select</code> shares his parts contract at <code>@skryensya/vanilla</code> and <code>@skryensya/react</code>; The machine of each binding is an internal detail.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a standard form choice, use the <a href="#native-select">native Select</a> documented at the end: it does not load an enhancer, preserves platform behavior, and styles its picker through progressive enhancement.
  </p>

  <ComponentPreview tree={selectTree(t)} label="Select enhanced" viewport="menu" />
  <p>
    Density compacts the space around the selector, not its tactile targets: the trigger and each option remain a minimum of <code>44px</code> high.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={styles} label="CSS" lang="css" />

  <h2>Authored HTML</h2>
  <p>
    The <strong>items are</strong> the collection: the enhancer reads them from the DOM, just as tabs read their triggers. Each <code>data-sk-select-item</code> needs one <code>data-value</code>. The full markup is in the <strong>Vanilla</strong> tab of the preview.
  </p>

  <h2>Initialize Vanilla</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={js} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>Listen to the change</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={listen} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>Forms and fallback without JavaScript</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={forms} label="HTML" />

  <h2>Enhanced contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The root carries <code>data-sk-select</code> and the documented part anatomy.</li>
    <li>The enhancer does not render markup or invent classes; only connects authored nodes.</li>
    <li>The value text is owned by the machine; placeholder, options and ids remain the consumer's.</li>
    <li>React renders the same contract and does not hydrate the vanilla markup.</li>
  </ul>

  <StylingHooks groups={[
      { file: "components/select.css", probe: "sk-select" },
      { file: "patterns/anchored.css", probe: "sk-anchored", title: "Anchor Inherits" },
    ]} />

  <h2 id="native-select">Native Select</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    It is a real <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>: selection, keyboarding, form submission, and accessibility still belong to the browser. skryensya/ui applies <code>sk-select-native</code>; there is no <code>data-sk-*</code>, machine or package <code>@skryensya/vanilla</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use for a standard choice. Choose Select enhanced only when you need controlled collection, item markup, positioning or <code>sk-value-change</code> event; appearance is no longer a reason to replace the native control.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview tree={selectNativeTree(t)} label="Native Select" viewport="menu" />

  <h3>Progressive enhancement</h3>
  <p>
    If the browser supports <code>appearance: base-select</code> and <code>:: picker(select)</code>, Core applies the same surface, spacing, states, and icons to the field, picker, and their options that Select uses. Other browsers ignore this block and retain the classic popup of the operating system. The HTML and behavior do not change.
  </p>

  <h3>Install only the native Select</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={nativeInstall} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={styles} label="CSS" lang="css" />

  <h3>Native contract</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Use an associated <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> or equivalent accessible name.</li>
    <li><code>form</code> selection, keyboard, and serialization belong to the browser.</li>
    <li><code>disabled</code> is the native attribute; It is not replaced by JavaScript state.</li>
    <li>Customizable select uniforms the picker; the classic popup is still the fallback.</li>
  </ul>

  <StylingHooks groups={[{ file: "components/select.css", probe: "sk-select-native" }]} />
</Base>
